2000-06-19  Stephan Nedregaard  <stephan@micropop.com>

	* src/liboe.c: BUG FIXING (OE4 SUPPORT)
	An unexpected bug lead to some messages starting
	with the last string from the previous message.
	This bug has now been corrected, the program has
	been tested with relatively large OE4 boxes...
	Time to release 0.92.

2000-06-17  Stephan Nedregaard  <stephan@micropop.com>

	* src/oe2mbx.c: WINDOWS COMPATIBILITY (for 1.21)
	Minor modfifications, none of which mean anything to 
	Linux users. oe2mbx now compiles on Windows and 
	successfully converted both OE5 and OE4 mailboxes.

	* src/liboe.c: WINDOWS COMPATIBILITY (for 0.92)
	Added Windows source compatibility. 

	* src/liboe.c: ADDED OE4 FORMAT (oe_readbox_oe4) (for 0.92)
	Provides experimental support for OE4 mailboxes. Reads 
	mailbox files (*.mbx), doesn't care about index files 
	(*.idx), as it's easier not to. Never call this directly, 
	oe_readbox automatically detects OE4 boxes when it is 
	detected that the box is not an OE5 mailbox.





	